WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.876
- That was ridiculous.

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:03.545
- Are you an athlete, Lefkoe?
- Not really.

00:00:03.545 --> 00:00:05.630
- Let me see you just
naturally come through

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.924
like you got a ball in your hand
right here?

00:00:07.924 --> 00:00:09.592
- Not time to panic yet.

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:11.928
- He should probably panic
a little bit.

00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:15.432
♪♪♪

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:17.726
[Cheering]

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:21.896
- Let's go! Let's go!
Let's go!

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:25.483
Welcome to
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe: The Show"!

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.527
The homies have arrived.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:31.364
They're havin' a good time
live at Dantanna's in Atlanta.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.824
And Simms.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:34.826
- Derwin's over here like,
"Look at all you crazy people.

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:35.994
What's goin' on here?"

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:37.662
- We got ourselves
somebody special

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:41.374
an All-Pro safety
in his very first season.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.960
He said, "You're not gonna
take me till 17?

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.754
Then I'm gonna smash it
in your face."

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.506
Cuz it's Derwin James.
Can I get more for the man?

00:00:48.506 --> 00:00:50.175
[Cheering]

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.260
- Uh!
- Yes, sir.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.470
What up, man?

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.055
- So why is the NFL
so easy to you?

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.431
- I mean, it's not easy, man.
- [Laughing]

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:59.726
- It's not easy at all, man,
but it's fun, you know

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.644
bein' able to go out there
and make plays on Sunday.

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:02.937
So it's a lot of fun.

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:05.565
- All right, so,
two teams in the Super Bowl

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.025
two teams that beat
the Chargers.

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:08.610
Not a lot of teams have beat
the Chargers this year.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.862
And I'm not tryin' to come out
with the negative stuff.
- Oh my God.

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:13.406
- No, but the truth is, is like

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.408
you're gonna know these teams
better than any of us.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.826
And I'm curious.

00:01:16.826 --> 00:01:18.995
Did you think that these were
two of the best teams you faced?

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:20.872
And what did you learn
about them facing them?

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:22.123
- Yeah, I feel like
those two teams

00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:24.459
were two of the best teams
that we faced this year.

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:26.544
I feel like Tom Brady—

00:01:26.544 --> 00:01:28.797
They're not gonna wow you
with the athletes and stuff

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:30.882
but I feel like they come out,
execute every game

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:32.092
and they're gonna be
what they need to be.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.134
And then the Rams

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:34.511
they have game-changing players

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.012
like Aaron Donald
and Todd Gurley.

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.430
So it's two different teams.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.391
But if I had to
pick, I'd say the Patriots win.

00:01:40.391 --> 00:01:41.810
- New England whupped you guys
pretty good.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.144
- That was a good whuppin'.

00:01:43.144 --> 00:01:44.395
- Yeah, that was a good whuppin'.
- Yeah, a good whuppin'.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:46.106
But what was
that experience like?

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.816
Just, I mean—
- To see that machine.

00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:50.026
- The machine.
Go up into Foxborough.

00:01:50.026 --> 00:01:52.612
I'm sure they were yellin' a lot
of creative stuff at you guys.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.988
- Yeah.

00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:56.616
- And did you get, like,
in awe of Brady or them at all

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.742
throughout the game?

00:01:57.742 --> 00:01:59.410
- I mean, goin' against Brady,
it was fun

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.703
cuz like I said,
they came out

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:02.413
they had a good game plan,
they executed.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:05.542
And we didn't come out
and play in the first half

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:07.001
and then we got down too far.

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:09.129
And, like I say,
you're not gonna come back

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.255
once he gets a lead on you
like that.

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:11.965
- Are you the most famous James
in L.A—

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.591
- Who, me?
- Playing sports?

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:14.509
- [Laughing]

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:15.468
- I might be, man.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.594
Hey, I might be.
I don't know.

00:02:16.594 --> 00:02:17.595
But King James

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:19.097
we got a good race
goin' right now.

00:02:19.097 --> 00:02:21.516
- All right.
- So, I was watching, like

00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:24.144
your IG and stuff
from the Pro Bowl

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.396
and I'm seeing all these
great players on the field.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:27.605
I'm seeing, like,
you and Keenan Allen

00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:28.815
and Jalen Ramsey.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.275
And I'm curious,
if you could make

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:33.319
Derwin James' best secondary

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:36.614
two corners, another safety,
and you

00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:39.075
who would be your—
and not including Chargers.

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:41.161
So we don't—
Sorry, teammates.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.162
- No Chargers?
- No Chargers.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:44.497
Who would be
your ultimate secondary?

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.833
- I say Jalen at one corner.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.460
I'd have to go Patrick Peterson
probably at another corner.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.254
And I'd put me and Jamal
back there.

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:52.130
- Jamal Adams.
- Jamal Adams.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.299
- The two 33s back there.
- Yeah, 33s back there.

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:56.718
- Is there—
cuz I feel like you guys

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:59.053
you're gonna be competing
for All-Pro spots

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:00.221
and all that.

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:02.432
But I feel like you guys
play so similar.

00:03:02.432 --> 00:03:04.225
Is there, like,
a friendship there too?

00:03:04.225 --> 00:03:05.810
- Yeah, we got
a great friendship.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:06.936
I mean, we've grown

00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:09.147
over the last year
of knowing each other.

00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:10.607
We respect each other game

00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:12.317
and I feel like
he gonna do great things

00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:14.194
and I'm gonna do great things
in this league.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:17.280
- We have a number
of meaningless debates

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.199
that I would like you
to help us settle.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:20.658
I don't know
what side you're on.

00:03:20.658 --> 00:03:21.868
I don't know
what side you're on.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.161
I don't even know
what side I'm on.

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:26.331
Waffle House at 2 p.m.
or 2 a.m.?

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:27.790
- A.M.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.292
- Yeah! A.M.!

00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:30.210
- A.M., come on. A.M.!

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.211
- I'm just sayin' this right now.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.670
- Waffle House for the game!

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.131
- I kinda feel grimy
when I go there at 2 p.m.

00:03:35.131 --> 00:03:36.090
- Yeah.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.175
- I agree.
- Right?

00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:39.093
I'm like, "Ugh!
2 p.m. Waffle House?!"

00:03:39.093 --> 00:03:40.220
- Oh, you trippin'.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.596
- "What the hell
am I doin' in here?"

00:03:41.596 --> 00:03:43.014
- My girlfriend has never—
- 2 in the morning, man

00:03:43.014 --> 00:03:44.265
you good.

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:46.309
- My girlfriend's never been
to a Waffle House

00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:47.936
and she would go at 2 p.m.

00:03:47.936 --> 00:03:49.270
You don't wanna see it.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.605
You don't want the sun comin' in

00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:51.981
and see what the floors
look like.

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:53.483
- Nah, nah.
- No.

00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:58.196
This is a debate that we have
had on the podcast forever.

00:03:58.196 --> 00:04:00.365
If there was a fight

00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:04.327
between a grizzly bear
and a lion

00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:05.870
who would win that fight?

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.330
- A lion.
- A lion?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.581
So you're Team Simms.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.833
I believe that the bear—
- Why?

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:12.168
- Would destroy the lion.
- Why?

00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:15.296
- Because the lion can only
attack straightforward.

00:04:15.296 --> 00:04:17.298
And even if he bites the bear

00:04:17.298 --> 00:04:20.468
you have the monster bear claws
comin' down.

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:22.428
He can tear him apart.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.265
- But we have seen video—
- Yes.

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:28.101
- That the lion has
a hard time with the bear.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.185
It hurt my heart.
- Yes.

00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:30.395
- I watched it,
I had to put it down.

00:04:30.395 --> 00:04:31.688
I was like, "I can't see this.
- Yes.

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:32.897
- It's hurting me."
- For real.

00:04:32.897 --> 00:04:34.315
- Yeah.
- It's been well-documented.

00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:35.900
- Because, like,
the lion is so muscular

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.277
he fatigues out.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:41.281
And the bear's so thick and fat,
it doesn't bother him.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:43.616
- The bear is like Fletcher Cox

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.910
and the lion
is like Derwin James.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.120
- Derwin James, right.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.539
- Eventually, he's gonna go,
"Are you done?"

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:51.332
- [Laughing]
- I ain't gonna get tired.

00:04:51.332 --> 00:04:53.835
- [Laughing]
- So, OK, new battle

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:55.962
Derwin James, Fletcher Cox.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.213
- [Laughing]
- Yeah, that's better, yeah.

00:04:57.213 --> 00:04:59.173
- How would you do?
- I'mma do good.

00:04:59.173 --> 00:05:01.092
- How many Fletcher Coxes—
- I like me.

00:05:01.092 --> 00:05:03.094
how many Adam Lefkoes
would it take

00:05:03.094 --> 00:05:04.512
to beat up Fletcher Cox?

00:05:04.512 --> 00:05:05.763
- How many?
- How many of me would—

00:05:05.763 --> 00:05:07.557
- They don't got enough,
I don't feel like.

00:05:07.557 --> 00:05:08.558
[Laughing]

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:10.435
They don't make enough.
- Four?

00:05:10.435 --> 00:05:11.561
- No.
- OK.

00:05:11.561 --> 00:05:12.895
- I don't think four would do it.

00:05:12.895 --> 00:05:14.147
- No, obviously not.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.440
- I think five, maybe.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.899
- I think 12
is the number I was thinking.

00:05:16.899 --> 00:05:20.945
- I think if we had
one Lefkoe on each limb

00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:22.530
and then a fifth one

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.032
to finally go to the body
and the head—
- No.

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:25.033
- You'd have a chance.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.243
- You're overestimating me,
very much.

00:05:27.243 --> 00:05:29.037
All right, can we get
a round of applause

00:05:29.037 --> 00:05:30.330
for Derwin James, please?

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.956
[Cheering]

00:05:31.956 --> 00:05:33.333
- Thank y'all, man.
- You're the man.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.959
- Appreciate y'all, man, for sure.
- Good luck to you, keep it goin'.

00:05:34.959 --> 00:05:36.461
- Yes, sir.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.087
- I'm J.J. Watt

00:05:38.087 --> 00:05:40.965
and ou're watching
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe"

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.718
[Cheering]

00:05:43.718 --> 00:05:45.928
- More, more, more,
more, more, more, more!

00:05:45.928 --> 00:05:47.889
Ohh!

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.474
Feels so good.

00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:51.309
The homies, the homies,
the homies.

00:05:51.309 --> 00:05:52.769
All right, well,
we gotta talk about the game.

00:05:52.769 --> 00:05:53.770
- Yeah.
- Sunday.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.021
- Yes.
- Patriots-Rams.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.189
I've never sat
this far from you. Feels weird.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.315
- I know,
we are really far.

00:05:57.315 --> 00:05:59.275
- What's goin' on over there?
- [Laughing]

00:05:59.275 --> 00:06:02.111
- So, the line,
according to Caesar's—

00:06:02.111 --> 00:06:03.196
arguably the best casino

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.031
I've ever seen
in my entire life—

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:07.325
is Patriots by 2.5.

00:06:07.325 --> 00:06:09.619
I wanna know
your last thoughts

00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:10.995
going into the game

00:06:10.995 --> 00:06:13.289
to aid my pick for this game.

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:15.833
- Right off the bat,
if you win the toss

00:06:15.833 --> 00:06:18.419
don't make the same mistake
Andy Reid made, right

00:06:18.419 --> 00:06:20.338
which was he deferred

00:06:20.338 --> 00:06:22.507
and kicked it
to Tom Brady and company.

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:25.301
Don't let New England—
don't let the train get rolling.

00:06:25.301 --> 00:06:26.803
That would be the first thing
I would say.

00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:29.389
If I'm the Rams,
I am gonna take the ball.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:31.682
You might go three-and-out,
whatever

00:06:31.682 --> 00:06:33.184
maybe only a first down

00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:35.311
but your defense
is gonna get on the sideline.

00:06:35.311 --> 00:06:37.480
They're gonna be able
to get geared up a little bit.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.148
And I would just worry about

00:06:39.148 --> 00:06:41.651
if you let Brady
and the New England machine

00:06:41.651 --> 00:06:44.862
and all their game-planning
come out the first drive

00:06:44.862 --> 00:06:46.489
and just,
"Oh gosh, here it goes."

00:06:46.489 --> 00:06:47.573
It's pulling guards.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.616
It's screens.

00:06:48.616 --> 00:06:50.243
It's Brady down the middle.

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.494
- And then the whole air
leaves the stadium.

00:06:51.494 --> 00:06:52.620
- The air leaves the stadium.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.288
- Cuz everyone's goin',
"Here's Tom Brady."

00:06:54.288 --> 00:06:55.748
- And the Rams are gonna go

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.625
"Damn, this is, uh—
we haven't seen this.

00:06:57.625 --> 00:06:59.293
I guess this is the Patriots."

00:06:59.293 --> 00:07:00.670
And I worry about that aspect.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:01.712
- And your big thing

00:07:01.712 --> 00:07:03.423
if the Rams
wanna have a chance

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.675
is they have to set up
on defense right away.

00:07:05.675 --> 00:07:07.844
- Yes,
that's one of my big issues

00:07:07.844 --> 00:07:09.679
with the Rams
in the Saints game.

00:07:09.679 --> 00:07:11.180
And it's been an issue
for them all year.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.515
And I know

00:07:12.515 --> 00:07:15.184
and Lefkoe pointed this out
with my notes last week

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:18.813
when the Patriots
see a flaw like that

00:07:18.813 --> 00:07:20.106
and they start
to go through a game

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:22.316
and they go, "Man, there was
60 snaps in this game

00:07:22.316 --> 00:07:23.776
and about 25 of them

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:25.653
the Rams were still
talking to each other

00:07:25.653 --> 00:07:27.029
when the snap was going on"

00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:29.490
New England is going to have
a package of plays—

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.993
- They did that to Tennessee
in the playoffs last year.

00:07:31.993 --> 00:07:33.369
- Exactly right.
Where they just say one word.

00:07:33.369 --> 00:07:36.456
Like, I say, it might be
"tequila," all right.
- Ooh, hey.

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:37.999
- And they're gonna say "Tequila"

00:07:37.999 --> 00:07:40.084
and they're gonna know
the formation to line up in

00:07:40.084 --> 00:07:41.919
and they're gonna know
the play they're running

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:43.463
and there's gonna be no talk

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:44.797
and it's gonna be
get up there quick

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.049
and Brady's just gonna
hit the guy in the butt

00:07:47.049 --> 00:07:48.050
and they're gonna
snap it and go.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.093
And all the sudden

00:07:49.093 --> 00:07:50.386
the Rams are gonna be
all flustered.

00:07:50.386 --> 00:07:52.388
And if they feel like
they get a little success there

00:07:52.388 --> 00:07:54.015
they're gonna keep
continuing to do that.

00:07:54.015 --> 00:07:55.558
So those are little things
I watch early.

00:07:55.558 --> 00:07:57.810
The Rams gotta keep it close
early.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.187
- It gets away, yeah.

00:07:59.187 --> 00:08:01.439
- If it goes 10-nothing first quarter,
night-night.

00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:02.648
They're in trouble.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.317
But if we get through
the first quarter

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:06.819
and it's 6-3, 7-3—
- Yeah.

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:09.030
- You know, anywhere in that range

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.740
then the Rams, I think,
got a chance.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:13.451
The Rams gotta get some stops
early on

00:08:13.451 --> 00:08:15.536
because if they are
on the field too much

00:08:15.536 --> 00:08:16.829
you guys have heard me—
- Yeah.

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:18.915
- I worry that the thinness
of their roster hurts them.

00:08:18.915 --> 00:08:20.458
- All right, talk about
the Caesar's line.

00:08:20.458 --> 00:08:22.043
We had a big competition.

00:08:22.043 --> 00:08:25.713
Can Adam Lefkoe,
the legend that he is

00:08:25.713 --> 00:08:28.049
throw the ball 50 yards?

00:08:28.049 --> 00:08:30.635
Vegas set the line at 50 yards.

00:08:30.635 --> 00:08:32.428
You said "over."

00:08:32.428 --> 00:08:34.222
And then I think you went out
there and you took the under.

00:08:34.222 --> 00:08:35.515
- Well, I thought you could get
very close

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:36.474
and I thought he would get it

00:08:36.474 --> 00:08:37.975
But as I got here
Super Bowl week

00:08:37.975 --> 00:08:39.352
I was like, "You know,
this is gonna be more fun

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:40.353
if he doesn't get it

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:42.271
so I'm gonna root against him."

00:08:42.271 --> 00:08:43.898
So let's go!
Let's get into it!

00:08:43.898 --> 00:08:45.733
- All right, so here it is.

00:08:45.733 --> 00:08:49.862
For the first time,
I reveal the 50-yard challenge.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.656
Oh my gosh.

00:08:51.656 --> 00:08:53.199
[Cheering]

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:54.450
So everyone comes to media day

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:55.952
and they make it
about themselves

00:08:55.952 --> 00:08:57.119
and they make jokes.

00:08:57.119 --> 00:08:59.080
We have credentials.
- Yes, we are big-time.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.748
- Serious journalism.
- Yes, official.

00:09:00.748 --> 00:09:03.042
- And we're here to see
if the Rams and Patriots believe

00:09:03.042 --> 00:09:05.127
I can throw the ball 50 yards.

00:09:05.127 --> 00:09:06.087
- Ohh!

00:09:06.087 --> 00:09:11.509
♪♪♪

00:09:11.509 --> 00:09:12.510
- Here with Johnny Hekker

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.303
who is kinda
known for your arm

00:09:14.303 --> 00:09:15.471
more than your leg
these days.

00:09:15.471 --> 00:09:17.848
- The best-throwing punter
I've ever seen.

00:09:17.848 --> 00:09:19.225
- Wow, touch that!
- Damn! Damn!

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:20.810
- I flexed a little bit.
- Whoo!

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.437
- So we were doin' a pod,
and he looked at me and he went

00:09:23.437 --> 00:09:26.148
"Lefkoe, I think
you can throw it 50 yards."

00:09:26.148 --> 00:09:27.858
- Gimme a throw. Try.

00:09:27.858 --> 00:09:29.569
- Like—

00:09:29.569 --> 00:09:32.196
That's all I'm gonna give you
is that motion.

00:09:32.196 --> 00:09:33.489
- I think he can.

00:09:33.489 --> 00:09:34.615
- That's a good endorsement
right there.

00:09:34.615 --> 00:09:35.825
- Yeah, I think he can do it.
- That's big.

00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:37.034
- I believe in you.

00:09:37.034 --> 00:09:38.578
- 50 yards?
- 50 yards.

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:40.538
- Running start?
- Crow hop.

00:09:40.538 --> 00:09:41.789
- Yeah, he can do
whatever he wants.

00:09:41.789 --> 00:09:43.040
- Whatever he wants?
- He can do a somersault.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.834
- I think you could get it.
- Damn!

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:46.043
- I don't like—
I don't think so.

00:09:46.043 --> 00:09:47.044
- You don't think so, either?

00:09:47.044 --> 00:09:48.254
- 50 yards is not easy.
- No.

00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:50.131
- If you looked
a little more like Brady

00:09:50.131 --> 00:09:52.174
and my man Chris here, maybe.

00:09:52.174 --> 00:09:53.426
But you're too—
you know what it is?

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:55.136
You got too many muscles.
- He's too squatty.

00:09:55.136 --> 00:09:56.554
He has gotta—

00:09:56.554 --> 00:09:58.639
he thinks he can
throw the ball 50 yards.

00:09:58.639 --> 00:09:59.765
We just want—you think he can?

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:01.058
Size him up.
- No.

00:10:01.058 --> 00:10:03.102
- Just that quick?
- No! End it!

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:04.228
Do you think
he can throw it 50?

00:10:04.228 --> 00:10:05.354
- I'll give him 50.

00:10:05.354 --> 00:10:06.939
- You gonna look in his eye
and say that?

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:07.940
Damn, OK.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.191
Look at that motion.

00:10:09.191 --> 00:10:10.860
Do you think he can throw it
50 yards, Marcus Peters?

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:11.944
- That was serious.

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:13.446
- It's a different stroke
for every folk

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:14.572
so, I don't know.

00:10:14.572 --> 00:10:15.781
How many you got back there?

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:16.949
- What do you think?
Hekker said yes.

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:18.117
C.J. said no.

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:19.660
- 50?
- 50 yards.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.830
- I got you to the 35.
- 35!

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.665
- He's not throwing that ball
50 yards.

00:10:24.665 --> 00:10:26.083
- Yeah!
- You don't think so?

00:10:26.083 --> 00:10:27.126
- No.

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:29.211
- He thinks he can
throw the ball 50 yards.

00:10:29.211 --> 00:10:30.171
- Ain't no way.
- No way.

00:10:30.171 --> 00:10:31.922
- What?
- Ain't no way!

00:10:31.922 --> 00:10:33.090
- Ain't no way.
- He just looked—

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:34.884
- Ain't no way!

00:10:34.884 --> 00:10:36.427
- You ever play quarterback?

00:10:36.427 --> 00:10:37.386
- Like, with my friends.
- No chance.

00:10:37.386 --> 00:10:39.013
- No chance. Thank you.
- Damn!

00:10:39.013 --> 00:10:40.723
- What advice would you give me?

00:10:40.723 --> 00:10:42.308
- Don't overgrip the ball.
- OK.

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:43.351
- That's a good one.
- Don't overgrip it.

00:10:43.351 --> 00:10:45.019
- Right.
- Don't overstride.

00:10:45.019 --> 00:10:46.354
- Yeah.
- You can launch it.

00:10:46.354 --> 00:10:47.980
- If you get some air,
you might get some carry.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.148
- You might get some wind or—

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:50.858
- If you have the wrong
trajectory, I don't know.

00:10:50.858 --> 00:10:52.735
- Are you an athlete, Lefkoe?
- Not really.

00:10:52.735 --> 00:10:54.403
- Let me see you
just naturally come through

00:10:54.403 --> 00:10:56.030
like you got a ball in your hand
right here.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.448
- All right, hold on.
So if I was like—

00:10:57.448 --> 00:11:00.034
- You just went to catch it.
No chance you're throwin' it 50.

00:11:00.034 --> 00:11:07.750
♪♪♪

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:15.424
♪♪♪

00:11:15.424 --> 00:11:17.885
- I mean, 50 yards.

00:11:17.885 --> 00:11:20.096
It's far.

00:11:20.096 --> 00:11:22.181
Don't overthrow your first one.

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:24.684
♪♪♪

00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:27.144
OK, Lefkoe.

00:11:27.144 --> 00:11:28.270
45.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:29.355
- Damn.

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:35.653
♪♪♪

00:11:35.653 --> 00:11:38.239
- We're about 47-ish.

00:11:38.239 --> 00:11:41.242
Those last three or four yards
are very hard to get.

00:11:41.242 --> 00:11:43.786
- I'm channeling
my inner Nick Foles.

00:11:43.786 --> 00:11:45.621
No one can explain it.

00:11:45.621 --> 00:11:47.581
It's magic.

00:11:47.581 --> 00:11:50.501
Sometimes magic happens.

00:11:51.585 --> 00:11:52.920
Ah, s--t!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:54.213
♪♪♪

00:11:54.213 --> 00:11:55.423
Damn! Not that time.

00:11:55.423 --> 00:11:59.218
♪♪♪

00:11:59.218 --> 00:12:00.428
- Wow!

00:12:00.428 --> 00:12:02.346
48 yards!

00:12:02.346 --> 00:12:04.140
♪♪♪

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.642
- [Sighing] 48.

00:12:06.642 --> 00:12:10.396
I mean,
I guess I'm getting more.

00:12:10.396 --> 00:12:11.564
Ugh!

00:12:11.564 --> 00:12:14.024
Vegas always knows
where to set the line

00:12:14.024 --> 00:12:15.109
don't they?
- They really do.

00:12:15.109 --> 00:12:18.988
♪♪♪

00:12:18.988 --> 00:12:20.448
No!

00:12:20.448 --> 00:12:22.116
♪♪♪

00:12:22.116 --> 00:12:24.660
- 30 yards is your low
of the day.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.287
Not time to panic yet.

00:12:26.287 --> 00:12:28.956
He should probably panic
a little bit.

00:12:28.956 --> 00:12:34.420
♪♪♪

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:39.967
♪♪♪

00:12:39.967 --> 00:12:41.927
- What was that?

00:12:41.927 --> 00:12:43.262
- 49.

00:12:43.262 --> 00:12:44.638
- Are you kidding?!

00:12:44.638 --> 00:12:46.265
- So close.

00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:48.559
Want to touch the 50.

00:12:48.559 --> 00:12:53.314
♪♪♪

00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:54.982
I think that's all she wrote.

00:12:54.982 --> 00:12:58.819
♪♪♪

00:12:58.819 --> 00:12:59.987
- S--t.

00:12:59.987 --> 00:13:01.614
And now my arm's thrown out.

00:13:01.614 --> 00:13:03.240
My arm's dead.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:08.954
♪♪♪

00:13:08.954 --> 00:13:09.955
- That was a good try.
- Dang it.

00:13:09.955 --> 00:13:12.082
- It really was.
It was so close.

00:13:12.082 --> 00:13:13.584
I mean, you got to 49.

00:13:13.584 --> 00:13:16.045
You got to 40—
I'm not even gonna lie.

00:13:16.045 --> 00:13:18.172
I really didn't think
you were even gonna get there

00:13:18.172 --> 00:13:20.049
once I saw you warm up.

00:13:20.049 --> 00:13:21.759
- I tried.

00:13:21.759 --> 00:13:23.385
I thought I had it.

00:13:23.385 --> 00:13:25.888
But I guess I'm a 49 man.

00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:27.223
I'm just, you know—
- Yeah.

00:13:27.223 --> 00:13:28.307
- That's what I'm capable of.

00:13:28.307 --> 00:13:31.519
♪♪♪

00:13:32.102 --> 00:13:34.188
- Oh, man!

00:13:34.188 --> 00:13:36.315
- I'm just gonna tell you guys.

00:13:36.315 --> 00:13:40.486
To get to 49 is, like,
the most bittersweet thing ever

00:13:40.486 --> 00:13:41.904
so much so that I thought

00:13:41.904 --> 00:13:43.948
he was lying
about the half a yard.

00:13:43.948 --> 00:13:45.074
- He really was.

00:13:45.074 --> 00:13:46.325
He was like, "Are you lying?!"

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:48.744
And I was like,
"I would not cheat you."

00:13:48.744 --> 00:13:51.247
- I appreciate you guys.
I know you supported me.

00:13:51.247 --> 00:13:54.208
So thank you for helping me
try to get to 50.

00:13:54.208 --> 00:13:55.167
- Yo, way to go, Lefkoe.

00:13:55.167 --> 00:13:56.919
You're a good sport, man.

00:13:56.919 --> 00:13:58.504
No joke.

00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:01.757
- So next up, two guys
that could definitely

00:14:01.757 --> 00:14:03.384
throw the ball 50 yards.

00:14:03.384 --> 00:14:06.220
Two guys that think they're
better football friends than us.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.639
- Never.
- Chad Johnson and Terrell Owens.

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:10.349
- Never!

00:14:15.396 --> 00:14:16.647
- So you guys know

00:14:16.647 --> 00:14:18.482
that when it comes
to Best Football Friends

00:14:18.482 --> 00:14:21.652
Simms and myself believe that
we are the cream of the crop

00:14:21.652 --> 00:14:23.112
and we've looked
all over the NFL

00:14:23.112 --> 00:14:26.031
to see who can compete
with this connection.

00:14:26.031 --> 00:14:27.449
- Nobody!

00:14:27.449 --> 00:14:29.994
- But we found two guys that
wanna take the test, Simms.

00:14:29.994 --> 00:14:31.078
- Ugh!
How dare they?

00:14:31.078 --> 00:14:32.663
- Why don't you introduce them?

00:14:32.663 --> 00:14:35.624
- You mean Bjorn
the German DJ over there?

00:14:35.624 --> 00:14:36.667
- Yes!

00:14:36.667 --> 00:14:38.586
- Chad Ochocinco?
- Chad Johnson.

00:14:38.586 --> 00:14:40.588
- Bjorn the German DJ,
techno DJ.

00:14:40.588 --> 00:14:42.089
- No, you know what, I'm taking over.

00:14:42.089 --> 00:14:44.008
My name is Tommy Shelby.

00:14:44.008 --> 00:14:46.135
- Tommy Shelby, apparently,

00:14:46.135 --> 00:14:48.637
and we have
the Hall of Famer Terrell Owens.

00:14:48.637 --> 00:14:50.014
Terrell Owens!
Terrell!

00:14:50.014 --> 00:14:54.768
- Yeah, give 'em some applause.
- How you guys doin'?

00:14:54.768 --> 00:14:56.478
- So here's how this
is gonna work.

00:14:56.478 --> 00:14:58.439
We have a lot of competitions
to see

00:14:58.439 --> 00:14:59.899
whose connection is stronger.

00:14:59.899 --> 00:15:02.985
Not only that,
we also have the referee

00:15:02.985 --> 00:15:04.987
from the end
of the Rams-Saints game

00:15:04.987 --> 00:15:07.489
that decided
not to throw the flag.

00:15:07.489 --> 00:15:09.408
I'm only kidding.
I'm only kidding.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:11.535
It is our referee
for "Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:15:11.535 --> 00:15:13.287
- Go easy.
Go easy, all right?

00:15:13.287 --> 00:15:15.289
Look, you guys weren't there.

00:15:15.289 --> 00:15:18.459
There was a guy in the front row
making a hilarious face

00:15:18.459 --> 00:15:20.669
and I'm easily distracted,
all right?

00:15:20.669 --> 00:15:22.630
So just go easy.
- Awesome.

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:26.300
- He will be the arbiter to see
who is right, who is wrong.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:27.635
This is gonna get
very competitive.

00:15:27.635 --> 00:15:29.011
- Watch these two, ref.

00:15:29.011 --> 00:15:30.971
- I would say we could bring
Roger Goodell in this situation

00:15:30.971 --> 00:15:33.807
but he's of no use.

00:15:33.807 --> 00:15:35.601
- No comment.
- Oh, that got a lot of "oohs."

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:37.436
- I'm just saying.
- Are you guys ready?

00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:39.355
You got your game faces on?

00:15:39.355 --> 00:15:41.106
- Yeah, I'm just waiting
for the "Jeopardy" tune.

00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:44.109
- Here we go.

00:15:44.109 --> 00:15:47.905
In what year did Chad lead
the NFL in receiving yards?

00:15:47.905 --> 00:15:49.740
- Wow. Congratulations.
- What year?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.158
- I don't even know
if Chad remembers.

00:15:51.158 --> 00:15:52.326
- Don't look at each other.
Stay focused on the whiteboard.

00:15:52.326 --> 00:15:54.703
- Don't look at each other!

00:15:54.703 --> 00:15:56.497
- Write down your answer.
- We don't have multiple choice?

00:15:56.497 --> 00:15:58.624
- I don't even remember.
No hints?

00:15:58.624 --> 00:16:00.167
- No hints.
- Write down your year.

00:16:00.167 --> 00:16:01.835
Stop cheating.
Enough of this.

00:16:01.835 --> 00:16:03.337
- No, I don't even remember.
I swear to God, I promise.

00:16:03.337 --> 00:16:04.505
- Yeah,
so write down a year.

00:16:04.505 --> 00:16:05.589
- Go ahead.
- When you're good

00:16:05.589 --> 00:16:07.049
we don't keep up
with stats like that, bro.

00:16:07.049 --> 00:16:08.926
- Ohh, yes.
- I'm just sayin'.

00:16:08.926 --> 00:16:10.469
- I think I can lead
the league right now.

00:16:10.469 --> 00:16:12.304
- Right.
- With these damn rules.

00:16:12.304 --> 00:16:13.305
All right, never mind.

00:16:13.305 --> 00:16:15.057
- No looking,
no looking.

00:16:15.057 --> 00:16:16.266
Turn your stuff.

00:16:16.266 --> 00:16:20.270
- Flip 'em.
It is 2006!

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:21.563
- Are you serious?!
- Nailed it!

00:16:21.563 --> 00:16:23.941
- It is?
- Ohh!

00:16:23.941 --> 00:16:25.067
- It was?

00:16:25.067 --> 00:16:28.112
- 2006!
- That is ridiculous!

00:16:28.112 --> 00:16:30.114
- That's my dawg!
- What?!

00:16:30.114 --> 00:16:31.365
- That's my dawg!

00:16:31.365 --> 00:16:33.492
- That was some telepathic stuff
right there.

00:16:33.492 --> 00:16:37.371
- That's my dawg!
- What is T.O.'s middle name?

00:16:37.371 --> 00:16:40.040
- Ooh, I love this one.
- Well, we expect you to know.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.167
Don't tell him.
- He has to know.

00:16:42.167 --> 00:16:43.335
- Yeah.
- What?!

00:16:43.335 --> 00:16:44.420
- Did you see Terrell?

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.713
Terrell's like,
"Yo, that's easy.

00:16:45.713 --> 00:16:48.674
I already know my own middle name."
- What is his middle name?

00:16:48.674 --> 00:16:50.592
- And it's not "Handsome."
Just FYI.

00:16:50.592 --> 00:16:52.052
It's not "Handsome."
- Wait a minute.

00:16:52.052 --> 00:16:54.263
We haven't gotten that far
in our relationship.

00:16:54.263 --> 00:16:57.641
- That's why you're not gonna be
the Best Football Friends, Chad.

00:16:57.641 --> 00:17:00.019
- If he gets this, dawg,
I'mma fall out.

00:17:00.019 --> 00:17:01.603
- All right, Chad.
Flip it.

00:17:01.603 --> 00:17:04.940
- I went with what makes sense
to me, and it flows, you know.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:07.359
So if I was his mom,
this is what I would've named him.

00:17:07.359 --> 00:17:09.737
- Hold on, dawg, hold on.

00:17:09.737 --> 00:17:11.321
- You ready?
- Yeah.

00:17:11.321 --> 00:17:12.573
- Three, two, one.

00:17:12.573 --> 00:17:13.615
Flip 'em.

00:17:13.615 --> 00:17:14.867
- Edward.
- Edward.

00:17:14.867 --> 00:17:16.076
He does look like
he's got a little Edward.

00:17:16.076 --> 00:17:18.037
- So here's the deal.
- That makes sense, though.

00:17:18.037 --> 00:17:20.372
- Edward?!
- You got the first letter right.

00:17:20.372 --> 00:17:21.582
- You got the first letter.

00:17:21.582 --> 00:17:23.667
- Terrell's middle name
is Eldorado.

00:17:23.667 --> 00:17:24.835
- What?!
- What?!

00:17:24.835 --> 00:17:26.336
- Yes.

00:17:26.336 --> 00:17:27.671
- Like the furniture store?!

00:17:27.671 --> 00:17:29.506
- No. Like the car!
- Like the car.

00:17:29.506 --> 00:17:31.008
- Can we put, like,
an asterisk by that?

00:17:31.008 --> 00:17:32.301
Because there's no way
I would have known

00:17:32.301 --> 00:17:33.594
his name was Eldorado.

00:17:33.594 --> 00:17:35.471
- Well, if you have a middle name
like that

00:17:35.471 --> 00:17:36.513
you should have known that.

00:17:36.513 --> 00:17:37.848
That's, like, "Eldorado?"

00:17:37.848 --> 00:17:39.308
- There's a reason
he didn't tell me

00:17:39.308 --> 00:17:40.601
cuz I would have
still been making fun of him.

00:17:40.601 --> 00:17:42.478
- Exactly. Exactly.

00:17:42.478 --> 00:17:45.064
